[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Bounded expression admission and evaluation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EXPR-STRUCTURAL-LIMITS-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Validate every child within inclusive structural budgets
STATEMENT: >>>
Structural expression validation shall visit both binary children and reject
nonfinite constants wherever nested. Root depth is zero; depth64 and1024nodes
are admissible, while depth65 or1025nodes shall return InvalidInput. Structural
validation shall not invent an input to evaluate domain-sensitive functions.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: structural_depth_is_inclusive_and_counts_both_binary_children,
structural_node_budget_admits_1024_and_rejects_1025_nodes and
structural_checks_visit_nested_constants_without_inventing_domain_inputs.
Shallow full binary trees isolate node count from depth limits. Log(-1) remains
structurally valid while evaluation reports its domain failure.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EXPR-EVALUATION-DEPTH-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Retain recursion admission on direct evaluation
STATEMENT: >>>
The public expression evaluator shall independently enforce its recursion bound
even when structural validation has not been called. Recursion through binary
children and unary functions shall advance depth consistently. Selected finite
depth64 fixtures shall succeed and deeper counterparts return InvalidInput.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: direct_evaluation_enforces_recursion_bounds_before_returning_finite_values
uses right-nested addition/product, sine chains and exp(log(1)) pairs, with
positive depth64 controls. Fixtures remain mathematically finite to avoid an
unrelated overflow/domain rejection masking a missing depth increment.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EXPR-QUOTIENT-DERIVATIVE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Retain the analytic derivative of a nontrivial quotient
STATEMENT: >>>
For f(x)=(2x+1)/(3x+2) on the bounded tested interval[-0.25,4], the expression
evaluator shall return the analytic value and derivative1/(3x+2)^2 within the
fixture's1e-13 absolute value/slope bounds.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: linear_fractional_value_and_slope_match_the_analytic_reference;
64generated dyadic-input cases, Proptest seed2026111927. The positive denominator
avoids poles and the slope follows independently from determinant4-3=1. These
finite tests do not prove arbitrary expression derivatives or global accuracy.
<<<
